WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:03.130
INTRO:
Nvidia is one of the most underrated mega

00:00:03.130 --> 00:00:04.910
cap companies in the world.

00:00:04.910 --> 00:00:11.100
While Nvidia is extremely popular within gaming
and tech circles, the average person is not

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:13.250
so familiar with the company.

00:00:13.250 --> 00:00:17.900
This is quite surprising because unlike some
other background mega cap companies like TSMC

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:22.980
and ASML, much of Nvidia’s customer base
is everyday people.

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:28.319
Despite this, Nvidia was able to race towards
a trillion dollar valuation under the radar.

00:00:28.319 --> 00:00:32.390
At the peak, Nvidia boasted a valuation of
$867 billion.

00:00:32.390 --> 00:00:37.590
But, it looks like becoming a trillion dollar
company just wasn’t in the cards for Nvidia

00:00:37.590 --> 00:00:40.400
at the time given that their stock has gotten
obliterated.

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:46.400
In fact, since their peak in November, Nvidia
has sold off a painful 55% which correlates

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:49.950
to a market cap loss of $480 billion.

00:00:49.950 --> 00:00:55.440
By now, this is probably not even that surprising
given how bad the overall market is doing.

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:59.930
But, like all the other companies that have
sold off this much, Nvidia does have it’s

00:00:59.930 --> 00:01:01.570
own set of shortfalls and concerns.

00:01:01.570 --> 00:01:09.829
So, here’s why Nvidia is down $480 billion
and why it may be long journey back to the

00:01:09.829 --> 00:01:11.569
top.

00:01:11.569 --> 00:01:15.170
SEASONAL:
One of the biggest shortfalls of Nvidia’s

00:01:15.170 --> 00:01:18.969
business is that they’ve somehow become
a seasonal business.

00:01:18.969 --> 00:01:24.000
Now, this might sound a bit surprising given
that demand for their GPUs is rather constant

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:26.100
from companies and everyday people.

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:30.969
But, there’s also a third demographic that
you need to consider which is of course miners.

00:01:30.969 --> 00:01:36.170
If you’re not familiar with cryptocurrency
mining, it’s basically a super computationally

00:01:36.170 --> 00:01:39.359
intense process that validates crypto transactions.

00:01:39.359 --> 00:01:43.890
The people who validate these transactions
are called miners and they get paid for each

00:01:43.890 --> 00:01:45.899
block of transactions that they validate.

00:01:45.899 --> 00:01:50.359
Now, miners don’t have to do anything manually,
but given the high computational requirements

00:01:50.359 --> 00:01:53.850
to mine, they’re forced to buy extremely
powerful hardware.

00:01:53.850 --> 00:01:58.130
And as you guess, one of their top choices
is Nvidia GPUs.

00:01:58.130 --> 00:02:02.549
In the early days, miners didn’t really
influence the overall GPU market all the much

00:02:02.549 --> 00:02:04.389
as they were a pretty small community.

00:02:04.389 --> 00:02:09.560
But, as cryptocurrency becomes larger and
more people jump on board, it’s only natural

00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:12.500
that the mining community has also gotten
quite large.

00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:17.650
If miners were simply buying gpus on a regular
basis, this wouldn’t really be a problem.

00:02:17.650 --> 00:02:21.840
But, the interest in mining is highly correlated
with the bitcoin market cycles which have

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:24.090
thus far been highly seasonal.

00:02:24.090 --> 00:02:28.500
For example, let’s take a look at the 2017
Bitcoin cycle and compare it to Nvidia’s

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:29.500
net income.

00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:34.100
As we can see, Ethereum which is what people
were predominantly mining with Nvidia gpus

00:02:34.100 --> 00:02:35.400
peaked in early 2018.

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:40.670
This momentum along with the release of Nvidia’s
2000 series of gpus carried the company throughout

00:02:40.670 --> 00:02:42.080
much of 2018.

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:46.970
But as the hype surrounding the new gpus settled
down and miners flocked the scene, Nvidia’s

00:02:46.970 --> 00:02:48.790
net income got obliterated.

00:02:48.790 --> 00:02:56.510
Within just two quarters, Nvidia’ net income
crashed 68% from $1.23 billion to $394 million.

00:02:56.510 --> 00:03:01.340
It wasn’t till the last quarter of 2020
when Bitcoin returned to its all time high

00:03:01.340 --> 00:03:03.470
that Nvidia’s net income also recovered.

00:03:03.470 --> 00:03:08.970
Since then, Nvidia’s income has only gone
up, but as we saw in 2018, it’s takes about

00:03:08.970 --> 00:03:12.840
a year for the crypto cycle to reflect in
Nvidia’s bottom line.

00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:17.980
Also, Nvidia is supposed to release the 4000
series of gpus this year similar to the 2000

00:03:17.980 --> 00:03:21.980
series in 2018, so that should help hold up
their income for some time.

00:03:21.980 --> 00:03:26.000
But as we get into the end of this year and
especially the beginning of next year, the

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:30.820
weak crypto market will likely weigh down
on Nvidia’s income quite substantially.

00:03:30.820 --> 00:03:36.150
PERMANENT SEPARATION:
Even if the crypto markets do recover within

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:40.010
the nest 12 months, it’s going to be difficult
for Nvidia to maintain their current numbers

00:03:40.010 --> 00:03:42.910
because Nvidia and miners are slowly parting
ways.

00:03:42.910 --> 00:03:47.100
From Nvidia’s side, they’ve been limiting
the performance of their GPUs if they’re

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:48.240
used for mining.

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:52.350
The goal with this limit is to mitigate the
demand from miners and make more gpus available

00:03:52.350 --> 00:03:53.560
for everyone else.

00:03:53.560 --> 00:03:58.430
Now of course, hackers have figured out ways
to bypass these limits, but that’s besides

00:03:58.430 --> 00:03:59.430
the point.

00:03:59.430 --> 00:04:03.570
The point is that Nvidia is finally taking
action to limit the number of GPUs that are

00:04:03.570 --> 00:04:05.010
sold to miners.

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:10.160
This was something that Nvidia was previously
extremely reluctant to do for obvious reasons.

00:04:10.160 --> 00:04:13.970
However, Nvidia has been switching their stance
likely because they've realized that in the

00:04:13.970 --> 00:04:17.870
long term, they will lose the mining demographic
no matter what.

00:04:17.870 --> 00:04:21.370
And when that happens, they want to ensure
that they have a strong core of gamers that

00:04:21.370 --> 00:04:23.250
are still loyal to the brand.

00:04:23.250 --> 00:04:27.870
But wait a minute, why will Nvidia lose out
on the mining demographic in the first place?

00:04:27.870 --> 00:04:31.510
Well, the answer boils down to two reasons
starting with ASICs.

00:04:31.510 --> 00:04:36.190
ASICs or application-specific integrated circuits
are hardware that are specifically built for

00:04:36.190 --> 00:04:39.560
a given computational purpose which in our
case is mining.

00:04:39.560 --> 00:04:43.340
In the early days, mining ASICs weren’t
that prevalent given that there wasn’t much

00:04:43.340 --> 00:04:44.370
demand for them.

00:04:44.370 --> 00:04:49.180
But, nowadays, full on companies like Bitmain
have built on just selling mining ASICs.

00:04:49.180 --> 00:04:53.720
And given that mining ASICs are specifically
built for mining, they’re way better than

00:04:53.720 --> 00:04:55.790
Nvidia’s gaming GPUs for mining.

00:04:55.790 --> 00:05:01.091
Now, Nvidia has launched mining specific hardware,
so they might make a targetted move into the

00:05:01.091 --> 00:05:02.091
crypto market.

00:05:02.091 --> 00:05:06.840
But, the days of using gaming gpus for mining
are definitely coming to an end.

00:05:06.840 --> 00:05:10.070
Something else to consider is that much of
the crypto market is trying move away from

00:05:10.070 --> 00:05:12.960
mining altogether due to how wasteful the
process is.

00:05:12.960 --> 00:05:17.500
Afterall, to mine, you have to buy loads of
expensive hardware and constantly burn mountains

00:05:17.500 --> 00:05:19.470
of electricity to keep them running.

00:05:19.470 --> 00:05:22.950
So, cryptos like Ethereum are trying to switch
to a proof of stake model from a proof of

00:05:22.950 --> 00:05:24.169
work model.

00:05:24.169 --> 00:05:29.080
Both of these models are rather complex, but
all you need to know is that the new method

00:05:29.080 --> 00:05:31.580
does not require super powerful hardware.

00:05:31.580 --> 00:05:35.080
The founder of ethereum, Vitalik Buterin,
has already been trying to make this switch

00:05:35.080 --> 00:05:39.419
for years, and he may be trying for years
to come as well.

00:05:39.419 --> 00:05:43.390
But at this point, it seems like a transition
to proof of stake not just for etherem but

00:05:43.390 --> 00:05:46.090
cryptocurrencies as a whole is ineveitable.

00:05:46.090 --> 00:05:50.419
And as crypto and Nvidia sever their ties,
there’s no question that Nvidia’s financials

00:05:50.419 --> 00:05:51.590
will take a hit.

00:05:51.590 --> 00:05:56.590
Now, it might seem like I’m overstating
Nvidia’s dependence on mining, but this

00:05:56.590 --> 00:05:57.740
is not the case.

00:05:57.740 --> 00:06:03.050
In fact, the SEC just fined Nvidia for not
disclosing how dependent they were on cypromining

00:06:03.050 --> 00:06:04.610
to investors.

00:06:04.610 --> 00:06:10.190
Considering this, declining demand from miners
is by far the biggest threat for Nvidia.

00:06:10.190 --> 00:06:15.210
UNSUSTAINABLE PRICES:
Another major threat for Nvidia’s business

00:06:15.210 --> 00:06:17.810
is their unsustainable price increases.

00:06:17.810 --> 00:06:22.389
Over the past several years, Nvidia has enjoyed
extremely strong pricing power due to overwhelming

00:06:22.389 --> 00:06:23.389
demand.

00:06:23.389 --> 00:06:27.820
For one, miners are willing to pay way more
for Nvidia’s gpus than gamers because it’s

00:06:27.820 --> 00:06:30.480
an investment for them, not just entertainment.

00:06:30.480 --> 00:06:34.480
And secondly, the supply shortage and more
specifically the chip shortage has made it

00:06:34.480 --> 00:06:37.340
imposible for Nvidia to keep up with demand.

00:06:37.340 --> 00:06:42.350
This deadly combination has led to gpus selling
for unreal amounts on secondary markets.

00:06:42.350 --> 00:06:45.290
Take the RTX 3090 for example.

00:06:45.290 --> 00:06:48.550
The RTX 3090 launched with a sticker price
of $1500.

00:06:48.550 --> 00:06:52.810
This itself is super expensive until you take
a look at how much these gpus are selling

00:06:52.810 --> 00:06:54.910
for on secondary markets.

00:06:54.910 --> 00:07:01.720
This listing for example comes in at an eyewatering
$4800 or over 3 times the launch price.

00:07:01.720 --> 00:07:05.900
Now, given that this is the resale market,
Nvidia doesn’t actually make anything from

00:07:05.900 --> 00:07:07.780
these ludicrous resale prices.

00:07:07.780 --> 00:07:12.620
However, this has allowed Nvidia to substantially
raise the launch prices of their new gpus.

00:07:12.620 --> 00:07:19.340
For example, in 2017, Nvidia’s flagship
GPU, the GTX 1080 TI, launched for $700.

00:07:19.340 --> 00:07:24.470
Last year, Nvidia launched the 3000 series
equivalent, the 3080 TI, for $1200.

00:07:24.470 --> 00:07:29.880
This means that Nvidia was able to raise prices
by 71% within a matter of 4 years, and that’s

00:07:29.880 --> 00:07:31.640
not even considering their new additions.

00:07:31.640 --> 00:07:36.120
You see, Nvidia had so much demand that they
decided to launch even higher end consumer

00:07:36.120 --> 00:07:39.310
gpus called the 3090 and 3090 ti.

00:07:39.310 --> 00:07:43.870
And the launch price of the 3090 ti is a whopping
$2000.

00:07:43.870 --> 00:07:49.580
This means that Nvidia’s flagship consumer
gpu has risen from $700 to $2000 within 5

00:07:49.580 --> 00:07:50.580
years.

00:07:50.580 --> 00:07:54.770
Clearly, gpu prices have gotten way out of
hand and they’ve been like this for years

00:07:54.770 --> 00:07:55.770
at this point.

00:07:55.770 --> 00:08:00.620
But, eventually, things will cool down like
they always do and Nvidia will lose pricing

00:08:00.620 --> 00:08:01.620
power.

00:08:01.620 --> 00:08:05.900
I mean, even Apple had to reduce the launch
price of their iPhones with the iPhone 11.

00:08:05.900 --> 00:08:09.730
And Apple had only raised the launch price
of their iphone by $100.

00:08:09.730 --> 00:08:15.150
Nvidia is over here raising prices $500, so
it’s no wonder that investors are worried

00:08:15.150 --> 00:08:18.030
about Nvidia's pricing power in the future.

00:08:18.030 --> 00:08:23.110
UNSUSTAINABLE VALUATION:
It’s not just Nvidia’s customers that

00:08:23.110 --> 00:08:25.490
have been willing to pay any price for their
gpus.

00:08:25.490 --> 00:08:30.210
Till recently, Nvidia’s investors were also
willing to pay any price for Nvidia stock.

00:08:30.210 --> 00:08:34.750
In fact, I don’t think it’s a stretch
to say that Nvidia had the richest valuation

00:08:34.750 --> 00:08:37.060
on the entire stock market.

00:08:37.060 --> 00:08:41.000
For example, if we take a look at their PE
ratio or their price to earnings ratio, they

00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:44.790
were floating at 70 to 80 for much of 2020
and 2021.

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:49.070
For perspective, Apple is trading at a pe
ratio in the mid 20s and Micorosft is trading

00:08:49.070 --> 00:08:51.190
at a pe ratio in the high 20s.

00:08:51.190 --> 00:08:56.029
Now, this is not actually that bad when you
compare it to Tesla which peaked at a PE ratio

00:08:56.029 --> 00:08:57.029
over 1000.

00:08:57.029 --> 00:08:58.029
But, here’s the key difference.

00:08:58.029 --> 00:09:03.779
Tesla was barely profitable with a net margin
of just 2.29% while Nvidia was at peak profitability

00:09:03.779 --> 00:09:06.820
with a net margin of over 30%.

00:09:06.820 --> 00:09:10.730
This means that Tesla’s PE ratio was super
skewed due to low profits while Nvidia’s

00:09:10.730 --> 00:09:13.450
PE ratio wasn’t skewed at all.

00:09:13.450 --> 00:09:17.650
And this becomes super clear when we compare
the price to sales ratio of the two companies.

00:09:17.650 --> 00:09:24.210
Tesla’s PS ratio peaked at 23.75 while Nvidia’s
PS ratio ran all the way to 26.62.

00:09:24.210 --> 00:09:28.670
Also, let’s not forget that Tesla is the
most hyped stock on the market.

00:09:28.670 --> 00:09:33.860
But somehow, Nvidia was even more richly valued
despite having far inferior growth prospects.

00:09:33.860 --> 00:09:38.740
Also, the recent sell off hasn’t made their
valuation that much better.

00:09:38.740 --> 00:09:44.650
Nvidia still has a PE ratio of nearly 50 and
a market cap of $460 billion.

00:09:44.650 --> 00:09:48.440
And thus far, Nvidia has only been reporting
stellar quarters.

00:09:48.440 --> 00:09:53.210
Imagine if Nvidia has just one quarter of
stagnation or even a decline.

00:09:53.210 --> 00:09:57.050
Their current valuation would just become
even less justified causing investors to sell

00:09:57.050 --> 00:09:59.070
off the stock even further.

00:09:59.070 --> 00:10:03.570
And don’t think that just because Nvidia
has already dropped 50% means that they can’t

00:10:03.570 --> 00:10:06.420
drop much further because they definitely
can.

00:10:06.420 --> 00:10:10.601
If mining demand doesn’t recover and the
overall market continues to sell off, Nvidia

00:10:10.601 --> 00:10:16.020
can easily sell off 80-90% like it did during
the dotcom bust and the 2008 financial recession.

00:10:16.020 --> 00:10:20.840
Really, you don’t even have to look that
far to realize how much Nvidia can drop.

00:10:20.840 --> 00:10:24.180
Just take a look at Netflix or PayPal right
now.

00:10:24.180 --> 00:10:29.760
FUTURE OF NVIDIA:
At the end of the day, Nvidia has been propped

00:10:29.760 --> 00:10:32.920
up by a several factors for several years
now.

00:10:32.920 --> 00:10:37.620
First you had the 2017 bitcoin bull run, then
there was the 2021 bitcoin bull run, and now

00:10:37.620 --> 00:10:39.570
you have the supply shortage.

00:10:39.570 --> 00:10:43.800
All of these factors have given Nvidia an
unprecedented amount of pricing power and

00:10:43.800 --> 00:10:47.160
leverage which Nvidia has cleverly used to
maximize profits.

00:10:47.160 --> 00:10:51.740
But, as these temporary boosts start to fade
away, the short term future of Nvidia is becoming

00:10:51.740 --> 00:10:54.050
more and more uncertain.

00:10:54.050 --> 00:10:58.460
Combine this with the fact that Nvidia was
already one of the richest valuations on the

00:10:58.460 --> 00:11:02.580
market, and it becomes clear that Nvidia’s
50% sell off could just be the beginning of

00:11:02.580 --> 00:11:04.740
something much more painful.

00:11:04.740 --> 00:11:08.710
This isn’t to say that Nvidia is screwed
in the long term by any means though.

00:11:08.710 --> 00:11:13.089
Nvidia produces the best gpus in the world
and they’ve diversified into several sectors

00:11:13.089 --> 00:11:15.339
from machine learning to artificial intelligence.

00:11:15.339 --> 00:11:18.250
So, Nvidia is by no means going anywhere.

00:11:18.250 --> 00:11:23.029
But, it’s very likely that we start to see
declines in Nvidia’s financials as the GPU

00:11:23.029 --> 00:11:27.090
market finally cools down and miners move
away from gaming gpus.

00:11:27.090 --> 00:11:31.490
But if we look past that, I think it’s just
a matter of time until their dominant position

00:11:31.490 --> 00:11:35.760
and massive investments pay off and Nvidia
reaches a trillion dollar valuation.

00:11:35.760 --> 00:11:37.120
But that’s just what I think.

00:11:37.120 --> 00:11:39.290
Do you guys have an Nvidia gpu?

00:11:39.290 --> 00:11:40.290
Comment that down below.

00:11:40.290 --> 00:11:45.040
Also, drop a like if you can’t wait for
gpu prices to finally cool down.

